data: {"type":"streamAssistantItem","item":"event","value":{"event":"end","part":1,"content":{"type":"text","text":"**Canon**\n- **Asha Pell:** Born on Orin; moved to Vesper at six and grew up there. She keeps a small brass key sewn inside her left coat cuff. It opens the old lens room; only Iven knows she has it.\n- **Iven Marr:** Lost his right eye in the winter storm of 312. He navigates the Nightjar using tide charts, not magic. Asha trusts him with routes but doesnât let him negotiate contracts.\n- **Bren Vale:** Petrelâs captain; refuses to join the Lantern Guild because he distrusts Tal Renâs friends. His older sister Nessa cooks aboard the Petrel, without a formal wage; she keeps Button, a black cat, aboard.\n- **Nightjar:** Now carries letters from Vesper to Kest. Its AprilâSeptember Orin-to-Vesper salt route is retired.\n- **Lens room:** A rockfall sealed it in 318; nobody has reopened it, and it has no other entrance.\n\n**Unresolved contradiction**\n- Your notes place Iven and Sera in the lens room negotiating a salt contract in 320, despite the room being sealed and Asha barring Iven from negotiations. This remains unresolved; no explanation is established.\n\n**Unknown**\n- How the 320 meeting could occur, and whether Iven negotiated without Ashaâs permission."}}}

